<Group labelreference="L247" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Note: the idea is that the induced velocity and the thrust must match up. So given a certain propeller rpm we can calculate the thrust based on blade element theory (here, the analytical solution to the thrust is used) if the induced velocity is known. The induced velocity on the other hand determines the thrust based on momentum theory. Using both equations at the same time allows one to obtain the induced velocity v1 which is returned.</Text-field>
